From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] network: skip timesyncd server query when NTP is disabled

The Web manual-time setting disables systemd-timesyncd, removing its D-Bus
activation alias. Querying timesync1 then produces avoidable broker and
network-manager errors. Check unit enablement before the query and skip
only explicitly disabled or masked services. Preserve static NTP server
configuration, and continue reporting unexpected errors for enabled NTP.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD optional NTP policy]
---

--- a/src/ethernet_interface.cpp
+++ b/src/ethernet_interface.cpp
@@ -681,6 +681,31 @@
 ServerList EthernetInterface::getNTPServerFromTimeSyncd()
 {
     ServerList servers; // Variable to capture the NTP Server IPs
+    // Manual time disables timesyncd and removes its D-Bus activation
+    // alias. Do not activate it just to query optional learned servers.
+    // Check enablement rather than NTP synchronization or active state:
+    // an enabled service that failed must still report its query error.
+    try
+    {
+        auto stateMethod = bus.get().new_method_call(
+            "org.freedesktop.systemd1", "/org/freedesktop/systemd1",
+            "org.freedesktop.systemd1.Manager", "GetUnitFileState");
+        stateMethod.append("systemd-timesyncd.service");
+        auto stateReply = bus.get().call(stateMethod);
+        const auto state = stateReply.unpack<std::string>();
+        if (state == "disabled" || state == "masked" ||
+            state == "masked-runtime")
+        {
+            return servers;
+        }
+    }
+    catch (const sdbusplus::exception_t& e)
+    {
+        lg2::error("Failed to read systemd-timesyncd enablement: {ERROR}",
+                   "ERROR", e);
+        return servers;
+    }
+
     auto method =
         bus.get().new_method_call(TIMESYNCD_SERVICE, TIMESYNCD_SERVICE_PATH,
                                   PROPERTY_INTERFACE, METHOD_GET);
